cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Eliciting self-reports from AI systems: pilot data, codings and scripts"
message: "If you use this archive, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Spano
    given-names: Nicola
abstract: >-
  Ten runs and 896 interview sessions with language models from two model
  families, six of them pre-registered, testing a fixed schedule for eliciting
  self-reports. Includes every transcript with its request and response bodies,
  every coding pass with the span each coder quoted, the pre-registrations, and
  the scripts that produced all of it. There is no interpretability access
  anywhere in the project, so nothing here tests whether a report is accurate.
keywords:
  - AI self-reports
  - introspection
  - chain-of-thought faithfulness
  - model welfare
  - phenomenological interviewing
  - pre-registration
license: CC-BY-4.0
